  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_6c609b80f1314357b3c3501260396cf4",
      "statement": "The Bean Pydantic model captures `process` as a free-text field (max 100 chars, nullable) rather than an enum, because roasters describe the same process inconsistently and the raw label is the only ground truth available at scrape time; canonicalisation is deferred to a separate auditable mapping step.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/schemas/coffee_bean.py#L237-L241",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dd717dfe966da9f46b8c3dbd97c7b1e134cafeff0a04ec8180317ad66fb18eb:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71708d6d164c4a60ad341dcd8b1c11a6",
      "statement": "The canonical mapping file `src/kissaten/database/processing_methods_mappings.json` contains over a thousand entries, each mapping an `original_name` (raw scraped string) to a `common_name` (standardised canonical) with a `confidence` score (0–1). Multiple original names legitimately map to the same common name, but each original_name must appear at most once.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/database/processing_methods_mappings.json#L1-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5e5e3622a8bcf74277441432b930b9be8ce4b2367ec3e633a0c78f21d2f78255:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7b905ac826574843b2e7bdce1d6d3313",
      "statement": "The `ProcessCategorizer` class uses a three-agent pipeline (categorise agent, merge agent, conflict-resolution agent), all powered by the `gemini-3.5-flash` model, to build and maintain the mappings file: categorising new raw names, suggesting additional merges of existing common names, and resolving conflicts where multiple originals map to the same common name.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/ai/processing_method_categorizer.py#L216-L326",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c0bd3cd008b224d4517a8c9bdf19a9e60fb47939b47067536d32665ec8753a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_23d361c0be6d4d8fa9f365a509d146d7",
      "statement": "The `categorize_all_methods()` entry point orchestrates the full flow: load existing mappings, query the database for unique process names, filter out already-categorised ones, batch-categorise the remainder (50 per batch), detect and AI-resolve conflicts, then save and print statistics. Hallucinated mappings whose original_name was not in the input batch are discarded.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/ai/processing_method_categorizer.py#L612-L773",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b8be8a1a4cb5d90535835a34498092577260253378739bb0bd00ce53e8e0b8f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8b27d933345a4af8bbf67093855123cf",
      "statement": "The `validation_gate.py` module centralises the pre-load invariant check: it validates that the mappings file has no duplicate `original_name` entries (detected case-insensitively), distinguishing redundant duplicates (entries that agree on common_name — dead weight, not a bug) from conflicting duplicates (entries that disagree — a real bug that causes silent data loss in the dict-keyed loader).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/ai/validation_gate.py#L22-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:69a6aefd56d108f8085e3e3ec7e59d196a51b72f7b9c5777e0eeced46668e774:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc3fb9de650d4498b54b29e963067299",
      "statement": "Production loading paths (`load_coffee_data`, `refresh_canonical_data`) call the validator with `allow_redundant=True` so only genuine conflicts block loading; the `SKIP_MAPPINGS_VALIDATION=1` environment variable bypasses validation entirely for emergency recovery; the `validate-mappings` CLI uses the strict default to surface the full dirty state in CI.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/ai/processing_method_categorizer.py#L827-L861",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a3b938c72132e3f54746e8ddb193fbf29a479ab00ee0d3d9b1d75603b32b1ee5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/db.py#L1633-L1650",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:34a7e9190d5fd478e3f19352c16fbe52b9801b5f9791d7df80ecfa6026059bf3:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_99cda536d491422a9c4fab623e5ea88c",
      "statement": "`_build_processing_mapping()` loads the JSON into a case-insensitive dict keyed by `lower(original_name)` with the `common_name` as the value, mirroring the varietal SQL `LOWER()` join so a scraped process value with arbitrary casing resolves to the same canonical.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/db.py#L1463-L1498",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8cc75ff633757643d90e35197cc3387a99b4bf9a6518d24c004f30af6d2e8c9b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_abadf242dea248f5a588de48fb88d3e6",
      "statement": "During `load_coffee_data()`, each unique `process` value from the origins table is looked up in the case-insensitive mapping dict; if found, the `process_common_name` and `process_common_slug` columns are updated for all matching origins. If no mapping exists, the original process name is kept as the common name so unmapped processes are not lost.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/db.py#L2414-L2457",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54d40b4a6023b633a6d40aef493dfb0e6aa52cd796d8f49e9e50601f3d0cfc96:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7354f6009734b77926bbc20df3168bc",
      "statement": "The `categorize_process()` function in the API groups processes into eleven broad categories (infused_cofermented, barrel_aged, decaf, anaerobic_carbonic, advanced_technical, honey, washed, natural, wet_hulled, experimental, other) via priority-ordered keyword matching, with ordering chosen so multi-attribute processes (e.g. decaf+washed) land in the most distinguishing bucket.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L1157-L1240",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c4625ecbaed9197d7c2e85eccc7c28db05d88dd1e8330be88ec0e0f83b012c7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84f9118d3d7341eeafd5f5099ff9e201",
      "statement": "`GET /v1/processes` returns all processing methods grouped by the eleven categories, aggregating per `process_common_name` with bean_count, roaster_count, country_count, a per-country breakdown, the aggregated original raw process names, a slug, and the category. The endpoint is cached via aiocache's SimpleMemoryCache.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/kissaten/api/main.py#L5289-L5413",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c9fabc38100f0f43f96896d5f9731d8123c6ee4aa29ceed829bcdb83a2829b8b:"
        }
